# Team Dynamics & The Project Leader Role

<img src="https://images.code.org/6a8e08927dd4e103e973c3ffd85815d1-image-1776789357244.png" alt="group of students working on a kanban board" width="350px" style="border-radius:10px; float:right; margin: 20px 20px 40px 20px;">



**Team Setup**: Students work in teams of three.
.
**The Project Leader**: Each team has a Project Leader, which is a temporary role that rotates at each scheduled benchmark so responsibilities remain fair.
.
**Role Expectations**: The Project Leader is a facilitator, not a boss or a manager. They do not assign work without discussion or make decisions alone.
.
**Key Duties**: They keep the Kanban board up to date, check in with teammates about task progress, and help the team notice when tasks are blocked or finished.

> #### The goal of the role is **clarity and coordination**, not speed.

![]()
